1
00:00:06,860 --> 00:00:08,780
The leadership course starts today.

2
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:12,650
All of the class reps and event planners will be attending.

3
00:00:12,650 --> 00:00:15,620
It'll be an overnight training camp!

4
00:00:22,580 --> 00:00:28,340
Tanaka

5
00:00:28,670 --> 00:00:31,460
Are you asleep? Don't tell me you're still sleeping!

6
00:00:31,460 --> 00:00:33,760
Come on, Kou! Wake up!

7
00:00:35,220 --> 00:00:37,350
I bet you just got out of bed.

8
00:00:37,350 --> 00:00:39,760
I even called to make sure you woke—

9
00:00:43,060 --> 00:00:45,690
You're such a nag.

10
00:00:49,230 --> 00:00:51,280
Why are you naked?!

11
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:12,630
I didn't come here for that!

12
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:15,800
Huh? Is your brain working?

13
00:01:17,050 --> 00:01:19,800
Who would even want to lay a hand on you?

14
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:22,310
You woke the whole town up with your screaming.

15
00:01:22,310 --> 00:01:24,390
B-B-But, naked!

16
00:01:24,390 --> 00:01:26,480
I was about to shower.

17
00:01:28,440 --> 00:01:29,520
I was so off!

18
00:01:30,110 --> 00:01:32,360
Please just kill me!

19
00:01:33,740 --> 00:01:37,660
Wait, you're gonna shower now? There's no time!

20
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:39,450
You worry too much.

21
00:01:39,450 --> 00:01:40,830
Just wait in here.

22
00:01:40,830 --> 00:01:42,910
Then get a move on!

23
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:45,250
That hurt, you know.

24
00:01:47,620 --> 00:01:49,540
Kou's bare skin.

25
00:01:50,080 --> 00:01:52,420
I did not mean to do that.

26
00:01:52,420 --> 00:01:56,130
I-It was pretty smooth.

27
00:01:57,090 --> 00:01:59,840
Does he use product or something?

28
00:02:11,150 --> 00:02:13,190
It's really tidy in here.

29
00:02:22,740 --> 00:02:25,200
Kou 3 y.o.

30
00:02:22,740 --> 00:02:25,200
Kou 4 y.o.

31
00:02:22,740 --> 00:02:25,200
Youichi 3 y.o.

32
00:02:22,740 --> 00:02:25,200
Youichi 4 y.o.

33
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:29,170
I'm ready.

34
00:02:29,170 --> 00:02:30,880
Oh, right.

35
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:32,880
Man, that was fast.

36
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:34,130
Let's head out.

37
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:35,840
Cooking Basics

38
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:42,930
See? We made it with time to spare.

39
00:02:42,930 --> 00:02:44,810
Yeah, just barely.

40
00:02:45,350 --> 00:02:48,430
I like having a bit extra ti—

41
00:02:48,430 --> 00:02:49,310
What?

42
00:02:52,610 --> 00:02:54,860
I can't believe you left your bag at my house!

43
00:02:54,860 --> 00:02:56,280
Forgive me!

44
00:02:56,730 --> 00:02:59,570
Stop slacking, Kou! Hurry it up!

45
00:02:59,570 --> 00:03:02,030
Why don't you try running with this?!

46
00:03:07,370 --> 00:03:08,830
The train's leaving!

47
00:03:08,830 --> 00:03:10,620
Guess we'll have to wait.

48
00:03:10,620 --> 00:03:11,790
Let's grab the next one.

49
00:03:12,420 --> 00:03:14,750
Don't you give up on me!

50
00:03:18,970 --> 00:03:20,680
Made it...

51
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:24,680
Where were we meeting up again...

52
00:03:25,470 --> 00:03:28,980
Pretty sure it was Oosakigaoka Station.

53
00:03:29,480 --> 00:03:31,770
Oosakigaoka's in the other direction.

54
00:03:34,270 --> 00:03:39,240
I messed up! I got on the train
I take to school out of habit!

55
00:03:39,240 --> 00:03:42,910
This one's a super express train, so we'll be stuck here for a while.

56
00:03:44,620 --> 00:03:48,120
Sorry, Yuuri!

57
00:03:48,910 --> 00:03:51,580
Hello, Futaba-chan? Where are you?

58
00:03:51,580 --> 00:03:55,590
Sorry! I bet everyone's already there!

59
00:03:55,590 --> 00:03:59,550
Tanaka-sensei, I know that blaming you won't get me anywhere,

60
00:04:00,090 --> 00:04:03,260
but you need to keep a closer eye on your students!

61
00:04:03,260 --> 00:04:05,510
I'm really sorry.

62
00:04:05,510 --> 00:04:10,140
Well I'm not waiting! Tell them to find a map and get there themselves!

63
00:04:10,140 --> 00:04:12,690
Did you hear that?

64
00:04:17,320 --> 00:04:20,650
I feel spent already.

65
00:04:20,650 --> 00:04:22,950
That's what I want to say.

66
00:04:26,370 --> 00:04:28,200
Kou, go ahead and nap.

67
00:04:28,790 --> 00:04:30,580
You don't mind?

68
00:04:30,580 --> 00:04:33,830
Yeah, I'll wake you when we get there.

69
00:04:33,830 --> 00:04:36,330
I'll take you up on that.

70
00:04:40,050 --> 00:04:42,590
This girl's unbelievable.

71
00:04:43,340 --> 00:04:47,220
The world has fallen in love

72
00:04:47,220 --> 00:04:50,890
An arrow of light shoots through my heart

73
00:04:50,890 --> 00:04:54,190
I just want to understand you

74
00:04:54,190 --> 00:04:58,560
Won't you open up to me?

75
00:05:05,490 --> 00:05:09,700
A fumbled exchange of words leaves a little taste of regret

76
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:13,040
Enough to make me cry

77
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:18,380
I want to link my racing emotions to the beat of my heart

78
00:05:18,380 --> 00:05:25,510
and put it all in tune

79
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:31,350
I lost sight of everything but my goal

80
00:05:31,350 --> 00:05:35,020
and had something important fade away

81
00:05:35,020 --> 00:05:41,270
Let's start all over

82
00:05:42,530 --> 00:05:46,400
The world has fallen in love

83
00:05:46,400 --> 00:05:49,660
An arrow of light shoots through my heart

84
00:05:49,660 --> 00:05:53,240
I want to know everything about you

85
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:57,420
Won't you tell me more?

86
00:05:57,420 --> 00:06:01,040
One inch feels like a million miles

87
00:06:01,040 --> 00:06:03,960
as the days just seem to race by

88
00:06:04,630 --> 00:06:08,380
I won't and can't ever forget

89
00:06:08,380 --> 00:06:11,640
this brightest page of my life.

90
00:06:12,970 --> 00:06:17,440
You two... make sure this is the last time!

91
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:18,770
Yes...

92
00:06:18,770 --> 00:06:19,520
Right.

93
00:06:20,190 --> 00:06:23,270
Now get your butts changed and go get some lunch.

94
00:06:23,270 --> 00:06:25,530
I'm really sorry...

95
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:37,660
You two...

96
00:06:37,660 --> 00:06:43,710
When both of our class reps are late, we're the ones who look bad!

97
00:06:43,710 --> 00:06:46,590
Yeah... sorry again.

98
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:48,840
Kou.

99
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:53,010
You're going to have to write an essay reflecting on why you were late.

100
00:06:53,010 --> 00:06:55,930
Bring it in before lights-out.

101
00:06:57,730 --> 00:06:59,480
You too, Yoshioka.

102
00:06:59,480 --> 00:07:01,100
Uh, right...

103
00:07:04,150 --> 00:07:07,690
Christ, now I've gotta write an essay...

104
00:07:09,110 --> 00:07:13,820
When you cause trouble like this, it reflects badly on Tanaka-sensei as well.

105
00:07:13,820 --> 00:07:16,290
Watch yourself from now on.

106
00:07:16,870 --> 00:07:19,500
Whatever, he's fine.

107
00:07:20,290 --> 00:07:23,500
It's my business. He has nothing to do with it.

108
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:27,670
He has nothing to do with it, yet he had to apologize on your behalf?

109
00:07:28,090 --> 00:07:29,010
You child.

110
00:07:31,050 --> 00:07:32,510
No, wait...

111
00:07:32,510 --> 00:07:33,930
Spoiled brat.

112
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:39,140
M-Murao-san?

113
00:07:39,140 --> 00:07:44,980
O-Oh yeah! I was really surprised that you volunteered to be an event planner.

114
00:07:44,980 --> 00:07:47,070
Do you like this kind of thing?

115
00:07:47,070 --> 00:07:48,150
Not really.

116
00:07:48,940 --> 00:07:51,530
Then why'd you do it?!

117
00:07:51,530 --> 00:07:57,030
You've got a big mouth for someone so bad at talking to people.

118
00:07:57,030 --> 00:07:57,950
Hey!

119
00:07:58,620 --> 00:08:02,120
Don't talk to girls like that.

120
00:08:03,580 --> 00:08:06,000
Hey guys, let's all just calm down.

121
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,210
I'm finished.

122
00:08:08,750 --> 00:08:10,050
Same here.

123
00:08:10,050 --> 00:08:11,300
Huh?

124
00:08:11,300 --> 00:08:13,590
What just happened?

125
00:08:15,220 --> 00:08:17,640
Futaba-chan, don't let that get you down.

126
00:08:17,640 --> 00:08:19,720
Yuuri...

127
00:08:20,180 --> 00:08:23,850
Well, at least Yuuri's nice.

128
00:08:23,850 --> 00:08:25,270
That was good.

129
00:08:25,270 --> 00:08:27,270
What a wonderful meal.

130
00:08:27,270 --> 00:08:29,360
If you don't want it I'll take it.

131
00:08:30,780 --> 00:08:34,700
I was specially saving it for later...

132
00:08:35,570 --> 00:08:41,410
Curse you... I will have my vengeance...

133
00:08:41,410 --> 00:08:42,790
What happened to you?!

134
00:08:48,210 --> 00:08:51,170
Thoughts, anyone?

135
00:08:51,170 --> 00:08:51,960
Murao-san?

136
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:53,130
I have nothing to say.

137
00:08:53,130 --> 00:08:53,880
Yuuri?

138
00:08:53,880 --> 00:08:55,970
Huh? Um...

139
00:08:55,970 --> 00:08:57,220
Kominato-kun?

140
00:08:57,220 --> 00:08:59,930
Cool, orienteering tomorrow.

141
00:08:59,930 --> 00:09:01,220
Kou...

142
00:09:02,140 --> 00:09:05,730
No authority whatsoever

143
00:09:03,230 --> 00:09:05,730
They're so useless...

144
00:09:05,730 --> 00:09:11,230
Come on, say something! "What do you believe the purpose of school events is?"

145
00:09:11,230 --> 00:09:14,820
We might be picked to present on it later!

146
00:09:14,820 --> 00:09:17,320
Just write something noncommittal.

147
00:09:24,250 --> 00:09:27,670
Which class wants to go first?

148
00:09:27,670 --> 00:09:31,670
Let's see... how about 2-2?

149
00:09:34,670 --> 00:09:36,180
Futaba-chan.

150
00:09:36,180 --> 00:09:38,590
What, didn't you write something?

151
00:09:38,590 --> 00:09:40,350
Just say that.

152
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:46,440
Fun memories!

153
00:09:46,440 --> 00:09:48,900
What's wrong? Hurry up.

154
00:09:50,310 --> 00:09:51,770
Okay.

155
00:09:51,770 --> 00:09:53,650
Let's see...

156
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:56,530
In regard to school events,

157
00:09:57,910 --> 00:10:03,790
we believe that when students partake in events with objectives that can only be accomplished in a group,

158
00:10:03,790 --> 00:10:06,460
they will feel a sense of community belonging

159
00:10:06,460 --> 00:10:12,210
and be more inclined to cooperate with their classmates.

160
00:10:07,210 --> 00:10:13,250
I can't believe how well he can make stuff up on the spot.

161
00:10:13,300 --> 00:10:17,630
Very good. Next up is...

162
00:10:17,630 --> 00:10:19,090
Just a moment.

163
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:23,060
I don't feel like I completely understand your point.

164
00:10:23,970 --> 00:10:26,430
You are the biggest pain.

165
00:10:27,350 --> 00:10:30,440
Why do you believe cooperation is so important?

166
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:33,440
What? Well, that's...

167
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:40,410
Cooperation allows for accomplishments greater than those one can achieve alone.

168
00:10:40,410 --> 00:10:43,370
Fun memories!

169
00:10:49,500 --> 00:10:50,620
Kou?

170
00:10:52,540 --> 00:10:53,590
One day...

171
00:10:55,250 --> 00:11:00,010
One day, when we look back on this, I want everyone who shared this experience

172
00:11:00,010 --> 00:11:04,180
to remember these warm and fun times.

173
00:11:06,430 --> 00:11:08,140
Sounds good to me.

174
00:11:08,140 --> 00:11:10,600
You can sit down now.

175
00:11:12,980 --> 00:11:15,940
You look like a deer in headlights.

176
00:11:15,940 --> 00:11:18,280
You're the one who wrote it.

177
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:41,380
Yoshioka?

178
00:11:41,680 --> 00:11:43,760
You write your essay yet?

179
00:11:46,350 --> 00:11:48,970
Not a word, huh.

180
00:11:48,970 --> 00:11:51,310
Just write something noncommittal.

181
00:11:52,810 --> 00:11:55,480
You really amaze me, Kou.

182
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:56,610
How so?

183
00:11:56,610 --> 00:11:59,820
Everything comes so naturally to you.

184
00:11:59,820 --> 00:12:01,700
I try my hardest, too.

185
00:12:03,280 --> 00:12:06,530
It just always seems to come back and bite me.

186
00:12:07,700 --> 00:12:10,410
I want to be more like you.

187
00:12:11,250 --> 00:12:13,670
Why do I keep failing?

188
00:12:13,670 --> 00:12:15,000
I'm so frustrated.

189
00:12:20,130 --> 00:12:22,340
There's no reason to be.

190
00:12:23,970 --> 00:12:27,600
It's not that I'm good at things, I'm just noncommittal.

191
00:12:28,310 --> 00:12:32,060
You just see me that way because I couldn't care less.

192
00:12:34,650 --> 00:12:37,480
But the fact that you're so beat up over this

193
00:12:38,190 --> 00:12:41,110
is proof that you're not satisfied with where you are.

194
00:12:48,160 --> 00:12:49,080
So don't—

195
00:12:59,710 --> 00:13:04,930
A-Anyway, I think you've really got it all together.

196
00:13:06,550 --> 00:13:09,680
And you don't think you do?

197
00:13:11,020 --> 00:13:14,690
I'm just kind of good at going with the flow.

198
00:13:16,690 --> 00:13:18,810
The back of his neck looked as familiar as ever,

199
00:13:22,820 --> 00:13:25,990
but the words he said were not from someone I knew.

200
00:13:26,660 --> 00:13:29,490
I'm fine the way things are.

201
00:13:31,160 --> 00:13:32,200
For some reason...

202
00:13:33,370 --> 00:13:35,790
...I feel like crying right now.

203
00:13:37,370 --> 00:13:40,380
What made him change this much?

204
00:13:41,380 --> 00:13:42,420
I want to know.

205
00:13:43,550 --> 00:13:48,890
What happened to Kou in the three years we were separated?

206
00:13:50,850 --> 00:13:52,140
I want to know.

207
00:13:54,180 --> 00:13:57,690
How did he take all the things that happened?

208
00:14:00,190 --> 00:14:01,360
What're you doing?

209
00:14:02,400 --> 00:14:04,990
Just a second.

210
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:17,540
Hey, listen.

211
00:14:18,460 --> 00:14:19,460
Tell me...

212
00:14:21,540 --> 00:14:22,540
Do you love me?

213
00:14:38,350 --> 00:14:44,110
I want to know more about Kou, but is that love?

214
00:14:44,780 --> 00:14:49,070
Are my feelings towards the old Kou... or the new one?

215
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:54,870
D-Did you really just say that?!
How full of yourself are you?

216
00:14:55,490 --> 00:14:57,040
Don't be crazy.

217
00:14:57,040 --> 00:15:00,540
The only reason I asked was because you were stroking my head.

218
00:15:01,130 --> 00:15:04,800
Just so you know, I don't feel a single thing for you.

219
00:15:05,130 --> 00:15:08,670
You confused the heck out of me back there.

220
00:15:08,670 --> 00:15:10,760
I just had to make sure.

221
00:15:10,760 --> 00:15:15,510
I don't like how you are now at all either.

222
00:15:17,100 --> 00:15:18,020
It's just...

223
00:15:19,480 --> 00:15:25,730
When I think about how you used to be, I can't help but wonder how you, well...

224
00:15:26,690 --> 00:15:29,030
Something inside me just can't accept—

225
00:15:29,030 --> 00:15:30,990
You've changed just as much as me.

226
00:15:32,070 --> 00:15:34,870
Stop looking for the old me already.

227
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:37,700
It's just depressing.

228
00:15:41,670 --> 00:15:46,590
Also, for someone pretending to try so hard to move forward,

229
00:15:46,590 --> 00:15:48,510
you sure do cling to the past.

230
00:15:49,010 --> 00:15:50,920
You're pathetic.

231
00:15:54,050 --> 00:15:56,720
Wh-What the heck?

232
00:15:58,270 --> 00:15:59,520
I knew it...

233
00:16:00,560 --> 00:16:05,190
The Kou today is not the one I love!

234
00:16:19,910 --> 00:16:21,500
How immature.

235
00:16:21,500 --> 00:16:24,250
What, you two fighting?

236
00:16:24,250 --> 00:16:25,210
Not really.

237
00:16:26,460 --> 00:16:29,420
That's exactly the kind of thing a couple would do!

238
00:16:29,420 --> 00:16:31,300
Who'd go out with that?

239
00:16:31,300 --> 00:16:35,140
I can't tell if you're the same or total opposites.

240
00:16:35,140 --> 00:16:35,760
Right?

241
00:16:39,970 --> 00:16:42,180
I'm going to clean over there.

242
00:16:42,180 --> 00:16:43,770
What's with her?

243
00:16:43,770 --> 00:16:45,400
She clearly hates you.

244
00:16:46,150 --> 00:16:48,650
You're not really fighting, are you?

245
00:16:52,570 --> 00:16:54,320
My cupcake...

246
00:16:53,950 --> 00:16:56,820
Anger

247
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:56,410
Never forget...

248
00:16:56,410 --> 00:16:58,200
I'm fine over here.

249
00:17:02,160 --> 00:17:05,500
Go help the others, Murao.

250
00:17:06,120 --> 00:17:08,210
They have enough people over there.

251
00:17:09,340 --> 00:17:10,960
I'll stay.

252
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:16,180
Murao, you need to get along with the others.

253
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:19,810
You can't say that you're be fine alone

254
00:17:19,810 --> 00:17:23,180
until you've put in the effort to making a place for yourself.

255
00:17:23,930 --> 00:17:26,100
I am putting in the effort.

256
00:17:33,690 --> 00:17:36,950
Murao, I'm a teacher.

257
00:17:36,950 --> 00:17:40,530
I won't leave you as long as you're my student.

258
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:44,450
But in the same vein, we can't get any closer.

259
00:17:46,460 --> 00:17:47,960
I've told you that many times.

260
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:55,590
Murao.

261
00:17:58,180 --> 00:18:00,050
Go join everyone else.

262
00:18:21,620 --> 00:18:22,910
Um...

263
00:18:32,460 --> 00:18:34,050
Damn Kou!

264
00:18:36,010 --> 00:18:38,970
Why am I so pissed off?

265
00:18:39,800 --> 00:18:41,140
You're pathetic.

266
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:47,230
Oh... it's because he was right.

267
00:18:48,390 --> 00:18:52,360
He may have been right, but I'm
still doing my best to change.

268
00:18:53,230 --> 00:18:57,360
All I need to do is keep moving forward! Yeah!

269
00:18:57,940 --> 00:18:59,820
First, I should make up with Kou!

270
00:19:05,410 --> 00:19:06,620
Ah, Kou!

271
00:19:13,840 --> 00:19:16,300
I-Is she confessing to him?

272
00:19:17,010 --> 00:19:19,470
She totally is!

273
00:19:21,930 --> 00:19:29,100
He went and called me pathetic, and now he's grinning like an idiot at that girl!

274
00:19:29,100 --> 00:19:30,020
Hello?

275
00:19:33,480 --> 00:19:35,570
E-Excuse me!

276
00:19:35,570 --> 00:19:36,480
You a second-year?

277
00:19:36,480 --> 00:19:38,190
Well aren't you aggressive!

278
00:19:38,190 --> 00:19:39,650
Um, no...

279
00:19:39,650 --> 00:19:41,990
You're pretty cute.

280
00:19:40,150 --> 00:19:41,990
Crap, third-years...

281
00:19:41,990 --> 00:19:44,120
Oh, you must want to ask me out!

282
00:19:44,120 --> 00:19:44,660
Huh?

283
00:19:44,660 --> 00:19:46,030
No, it must be me.

284
00:19:46,030 --> 00:19:48,160
Doofus, there's no way.

285
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:49,200
Same to you.

286
00:19:49,540 --> 00:19:51,040
Then who's it gonna be?

287
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:52,170
Excuse me...

288
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:52,170
It's me, man!

289
00:19:56,670 --> 00:19:58,090
Sorry about that.

290
00:19:58,090 --> 00:20:01,170
This is my girlfriend.

291
00:20:04,180 --> 00:20:05,300
Well...

292
00:20:05,300 --> 00:20:07,930
We didn't really mean to...

293
00:20:07,930 --> 00:20:09,020
I see.

294
00:20:09,600 --> 00:20:10,350
Well then.

295
00:20:16,570 --> 00:20:18,530
What're you doing, stupid?

296
00:20:18,530 --> 00:20:21,990
It just kinda... happened.

297
00:20:21,990 --> 00:20:23,950
How does that happen?

298
00:20:24,450 --> 00:20:25,660
You're the one who—

299
00:20:25,660 --> 00:20:27,780
What? What did I do?

300
00:20:29,290 --> 00:20:33,960
Sorry. I was just trying to shift the blame.

301
00:20:45,140 --> 00:20:48,760
How long are you going to hold my hand?

302
00:20:49,140 --> 00:20:50,350
A bit longer.

303
00:20:51,430 --> 00:20:53,230
Just bear with it.

304
00:20:53,890 --> 00:20:57,190
I don't really... mind that much...

305
00:20:58,060 --> 00:21:02,990
But you might get in trouble... if someone sees us...

306
00:21:03,860 --> 00:21:09,240
L-Like... your girlfriend, or something.

307
00:21:11,160 --> 00:21:13,460
She might get the wrong impression.

308
00:21:15,420 --> 00:21:18,790
No worries. I don't have anyone like that.

309
00:21:20,130 --> 00:21:22,670
O-Oh, okay then.

310
00:21:22,670 --> 00:21:25,630
Huh, never mind then.

311
00:21:32,890 --> 00:21:33,980
I see.

312
00:21:35,600 --> 00:21:38,440
I feel like a load's off my shoulders.

313
00:21:38,940 --> 00:21:42,570
Huh? Why can a single thing Kou says

314
00:21:42,570 --> 00:21:45,360
make me depressed or relieved?

315
00:21:46,530 --> 00:21:49,030
Even though, right now...

316
00:21:49,660 --> 00:21:52,700
...I don't even love Kou or anything.

317
00:22:00,750 --> 00:22:05,880
In a town beset by a sudden shower,

318
00:22:05,880 --> 00:22:11,260
I say "See you later", and wave goodbye.

319
00:22:11,260 --> 00:22:16,730
As I watch you pass through the ticket gate, I think:

320
00:22:16,730 --> 00:22:22,020
"It never goes according to plan, does it?"

321
00:22:22,020 --> 00:22:31,740
Everything seemed incredibly fragile that day,

322
00:22:31,740 --> 00:22:37,330
but it passed, as days tend to do.

323
00:22:38,500 --> 00:22:47,880
The rails carry you away

324
00:22:47,880 --> 00:22:56,140
leaving me alone on our usual path.

325
00:22:57,270 --> 00:23:06,780
The words I prepared for you are so simple,

326
00:23:06,780 --> 00:23:15,490
so why can't I say them?

327
00:23:17,250 --> 00:23:22,460
Why can't I?

328
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:40,020
NEXT TIME...

329
00:23:28,170 --> 00:23:31,640
Hyper goin' now, yo yo yo!

330
00:23:31,640 --> 00:23:34,970
Super orienteering!

331
00:23:34,970 --> 00:23:39,310
Get 'dem points along the way!
